PROOF license and attribution
============================

PROOF is a modified fork of Inkscape (https://inkscape.org/), developed
independently of the upstream project. It retains Inkscape's licensing terms,
copyright notices, and contributor credits. See AUTHORS for the inherited
contributor list and individual source files for copyright attribution.
See CREDITS.md for project acknowledgments, major components, and format-research
references.

Most source code is available under the GNU General Public License, version 2
or later (GPL-2.0-or-later).

Notable exceptions are:
- all javascript polyfill libraries are CC0 / Public Domain
- some libraries in src/3rdparty (mostly GNU Lesser General Public License or Mozilla Public License).
- a few files copied from GIMP, which are available under GNU (L)GPL version 3 or later.
- a few files which are dual-licensed, which means that they offer the additional permission to alternatively use them under another license.

The complete application binaries are covered by the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later), as in the upstream project.
PROOF's name and branding do not replace the licenses of inherited code or
third-party components.

Individual files and third-party components
==========================================

The license of each source file is identified by its SPDX-License-Identifier
header where present. Full license texts are retained in LICENSES/, including:
- LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt
- LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt

Some files are dual-licensed, for example GPL-2.0-or-later OR MPL-1.1, allowing
a choice between those licenses.

Libraries also retain their own COPYING or LICENSE files in their respective
subdirectories. Those notices and terms continue to apply.

See also https://spdx.org/licenses/ for the full license texts, and https://spdx.org/ids for the standardized header format.


